\subsection{Kinematic interpretation of the JONSWAP consistency check}
\label{sec:jonswap-integrated-elevation-clarification}

JONSWAP supplies an elevation spectrum $S_\eta(\omega)$, not the acceleration
process propagated by the filter.  Under linear wave kinematics,
\begin{equation}
 A(\omega)=-\omega^2\widehat{\eta}(\omega).
\label{eq:jonswap-acc-from-elevation-clarification}
\end{equation}
Because OU--III defines $S$ as the third integral of acceleration,
\begin{equation}
 S(\omega)
 =\frac{A(\omega)}{(j\omega)^3}
 =\frac{-\omega^2}{(j\omega)^3}\widehat{\eta}(\omega),
\label{eq:jonswap-S-from-eta-clarification}
\end{equation}
which is, apart from phase convention, one integration of elevation.  Equivalently,
for zero integrated initial conditions,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\displaystyle
 S=\iiint a\,dt^3=\int\eta\,dt.}
\label{eq:triple-acc-single-elevation-integral}
\end{equation}
Thus ``third integral'' refers to acceleration, not to three integrations of the
JONSWAP elevation process.

At the PSD level,
\begin{equation}
 S_a^{(2)}(\omega)=\omega^4S_\eta^{(2)}(\omega),
\end{equation}
so
\begin{equation}
 S_S^{(2)}(\omega)
 =\frac{S_a^{(2)}(\omega)}{\omega^6}
 =\boxed{\displaystyle\frac{S_\eta^{(2)}(\omega)}{\omega^2}}.
\label{eq:jonswap-S-psd-clarification}
\end{equation}
Hence
\begin{equation}
 \Var[S]
 =\frac{1}{\pi}\int_0^\infty
   \frac{S_\eta^{(2)}(\omega)}{\omega^2}\,d\omega,
\label{eq:jonswap-integrated-elevation-variance}
\end{equation}
and fixed-shape JONSWAP gives
$\sigma_{S,\mathrm{phys}}\propto H_s/\omega_p$.

Inside the estimator, the OU chain instead has natural scale
$\sigma_{aw}\tau^3$.  The tuner-input scaling is already given by
Eq.~\eqref{eq:jonswap-ou-target-scaling}, and therefore
\begin{equation}
 \sigma_{aw,\star}\tau_\star^3
 \propto\frac{H_s}{\omega_p}
 \propto\sigma_{S,\mathrm{phys}}.
\label{eq:jonswap-ou-physical-scale-consistency}
\end{equation}
Equation~\eqref{eq:jonswap-ou-physical-scale-consistency} is a consistency check
between the OU state scale and JONSWAP sea-state similarity.  It neither implies
that the filter propagates JONSWAP nor derives the deployed adaptation law.
